          "type": "reasoning",
          "text": "So the situation is:\n- t1, t2, t3 programs don't even read argv (no CLI args needed — they read from stdin). Only t4 reads argv[1] (the radius).\n- No --help or --version anywhere.\n- No CHANGELOG.md.\n- No project(VERSION) — currently `project(inobitec_stud LANGUAGES C CXX)` with no VERSION.\n- vcpkg.json already has `\"version\": \"0.1.0\"` and `\"builtin-baseline\": \"1577...\"`.\n\nInteresting: vcpkg.json already has a \"version\" field (0.1.0), and the builtin-baseline is already pinned (she worked on it in 2026-09-28/29 per journal).\n\nNow I understand the full picture. Let me form my answer.\n\nThe mentor's instruction: \"Версионирование делаем... Раз у тебя уже CMake, сразу промышленная форма — таблица в § 4.8, строка «Версионирование»: версия в project(VERSION), --version у каждой программы, CHANGELOG.md. Для компонентов разберись, что именно фиксирует builtin-baseline в vcpkg.json, и доведи фиксацию до конца.\"\n\nSo the mentor's plan:\n1. `project(VERSION)` — put version in CMake\n2. `--version` at each program\n3. CHANGELOG.md\n4. builtin-baseline understanding + finalize\n\nHer question: should she do the bare version first (small volume) for understanding?\n\nMy answer, being critical and honest:\n\nKey insight I should give: The \"bare\" and \"industrial\" forms here are NOT actually a huge gap. Look at what § 4.8 actually says:\n- Голая: `kVersion` + `--version` + `CHANGELOG.md`\n- Промышленная: CMake `project(VERSION)` + git describe\n\nThe bare form's three components are: kVersion (constant), --version (flag), CHANGELOG.md (file).\n\nThe industrial form replaces \"kVersion constant in code\" with \"project(VERSION) in CMake\". But --version and CHANGELOG.md REMAIN. So the industrial form does NOT remove the flag or the changelog — it only moves the \"single source of truth\" for the version string from a C++ constant to a CMake variable.\n\nSo the mentor's plan is actually: keep --version and CHANGELOG.md (the bare-form pieces